# The saved token. This file IS the bot — never commit it. The `.tmp` is the
# half-written one: the state file is now rewritten on every ask, through a
# rename, so a crash can leave one behind.
.steel-state.json
.steel-state.json.tmp
# The Solana key this robot owns itself with. Worse to leak than the token
# above by a wide margin: a token is one agent, and this is the vault every
# agent this key owns stakes from — plus anything else kept at that address.
.steel-key.json
# A vault transaction this robot sent and has not yet seen land. Short-lived,
# and the thing that stops a re-run depositing twice.
.steel-vault-pending.json
# How this robot died, and the faults it survived. Its own history, never a
# clone's first commit — and the file somebody reads when an agent is not
# where they left it.
.steel-incidents.log
